; Engine configuration file.
;
; A stranger's project, not this repo's. No autoloads, no bus layout, no assets,
; no host scripts — the point is what the addon does in a project that did
; nothing for it (ADR-0194, CONTEXT.md "Stranger project"). Shape copied from
; `tests/stranger/exmateria_schema/project.godot`; this is that rig pointed at
; the SIXTH in-walk addon, not a sixth invention.
;
; THE HARNESS FILES KEEP THEIR REPO-RELATIVE PATHS in the staged project —
; `res://tests/stranger/<addon>/…`, not `res://…` at the root — so every quoted
; `res://` literal is true in BOTH projects and `tools/check_res_paths.py` stays
; green on a clean checkout. See the schema rig's project.godot for the full note.
;
; `config/name` is not decoration: `tests/stranger/shared/stranger_install.gd`
; reads it to learn which of the staged addons is the SUBJECT. This rig stages
; two — the subject plus the one `plugin.cfg` declares as a dep
; (`exmateria_platform`, for `JsonAsset`) — so "the only addon here" is not a
; reading that works.
;
; THE ADDON IS NOT ENABLED HERE, and for this addon that is the whole claim
; rather than a formality. `plugin.gd` does nothing on purpose: the almanac
; registers no autoload, no singleton and no editor UI, so a consumer uses it by
; naming `ExMateriaAlmanac` — the addon's ONE global (ADR-0244 dec. 3) — and by
; nothing else. A table that installed itself into the host would be a port.
;
; 🔴 THE THIRTEEN JSON PAYLOADS ARE INSIDE THE ADDON, AND THAT IS WHAT THIS RIG
; MEASURES (ADR-0244 dec. 2). Every database reads its table by a
; `res://addons/exmateria_almanac/...` path, so a stranger project that ships no
; `assets/` at all still gets working tables. Had the payloads stayed in the
; host, this rig would come up and every `_ensure_loaded()` would find nothing —
; which is precisely the silent-empty failure ADR-0146 dec. 1 ruled against when
; `fold_layer.tres` travelled with `Fold.gd`.

config_version=5

[application]

config/name="stranger_exmateria_almanac"
run/main_scene="res://tests/stranger/shared/stranger_install.tscn"
config/features=PackedStringArray("4.4")

[audio]

driver/driver="Dummy"
